Counterintuitive Coercion
=========================
[] == false => true
  [] becomes an empty string, then 0; false also becomes 0.
[] == ![] => true
  ![] is false, then the comparison follows the [] == false path.
"" == 0 => true
  The empty string becomes numeric 0.
"0" == false => true
  Both sides become numeric 0.
null == undefined => true
  Loose equality has a special case for null and undefined.
null == 0 => false
  The null/undefined special case does not extend to numbers.
Boolean("false") => true
  Any non-empty string is truthy.
